From 2626a38e006acbd40763d77e1b29fb7f6d3dbe28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A9 project <dmayala@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:47:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] pmdomain: qcom: rpmpd: keep genpd's corner across
 sync_state

rpmpd_sync_state() zeroes pd->corner for every domain that is off at
that moment. genpd does not know: its performance_state stays at the
aggregate it last set, and _genpd_set_performance_state() returns early
while that aggregate is unchanged. A consumer that got a default state
from required-opps at attach (genpd_set_required_opp) and is
runtime-suspended when sync_state runs (domain off) therefore has its
vote lost: on its first runtime resume rpm_pstate is 0, genpd restores
nothing, and rpmpd_power_on() skips the corner because pd->corner is 0.
The domain is enabled at corner 0 until the consumer happens to go
through one runtime suspend/resume cycle.

Hit by the DSI PHY's MX vote on the Hisense A9 (SM6115): the phy probes,
votes MX NOM via required-opps, is suspended, rpmpd sync_state runs,
and the first CRTC enable powers MX on at level 0 (inferred from the
code, not measured).

Still send 0 for a domain that is off, but restore the stored corner
afterwards so the next power_on sends it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/pmdomain/qcom/rpmpd.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/rpmpd.c b/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/rpmpd.c
index 5f55fc791..df5b665bb 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/rpmpd.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/rpmpd.c
@@ -1155,18 +1155,31 @@ static void rpmpd_sync_state(struct device *dev)
 
 	mutex_lock(&rpmpd_lock);
 	for (i = 0; i < desc->num_pds; i++) {
+		unsigned int corner;
+
 		pd = rpmpds[i];
 		if (!pd)
 			continue;
 
 		pd->state_synced = true;
 
+		/*
+		 * Vote 0 for a domain that is off, but keep the corner genpd
+		 * last set: genpd does not call set_performance_state again
+		 * while its aggregate is unchanged, so a consumer whose
+		 * default (required-opps) state was set at attach and that
+		 * is runtime-suspended now would otherwise power the domain
+		 * on later at corner 0.
+		 */
+		corner = pd->corner;
 		if (!pd->enabled)
 			pd->corner = 0;
 
 		ret = rpmpd_aggregate_corner(pd);
 		if (ret)
 			dev_err(dev, "failed to sync %s: %d\n", pd->pd.name, ret);
+
+		pd->corner = corner;
 	}
 	mutex_unlock(&rpmpd_lock);
 }
